// "Discard N" ([CR#701.9a]): the imperative YOU-form discard — you choose N
// cards from your hand and discard them ([CR#701.9b] — the affected player
// chooses by default). Mill/Draw's sibling on the discard lane: the keyword
// action as DATA — a `Composite` whose tag is `Discard(You, n)` and whose
// body DESCRIBES the chosen-from-hand Hand → Graveyard relocation (an `Each`
// over a `FromHand` selection). The engine does NOT run the body: the choice
// is BATCHED up front (one `DiscardCards` decision picks the cards) and then
// realized as N per-card `Act(Discard)` events — each individually
// replaceable/cantable (madness exiles ITS card only, [CR#702.35a]) and each
// its own "whenever a player discards a card" fact. The at-random variant
// (`FromHand(random: true)`) is `DiscardAtRandom`; the declarative-subject
// form ("Target player discards N cards.") is the `Discards(who, n)` macro;
// this is the bare you-imperative.
//
// Usage: Discard(1) -> "Discard a card." / Discard(2) -> "Discard 2 cards."
(
    name: "Discard",
    template: "discard ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Count],
    body: Composite(
        Discard(You, Param(0)),
        Each(binder: Existing(FromHand(count: Param(0))), effect: Move(It, Graveyard)),
    ),
)
